  "note": "How each key of colors and darkColors relates to the colour tokens in tokens.json. role is the token a key folds into and also the others its readers split across. from lists the themes in which the key is read from its role now, written by npm run gen:colour-tokens; a key without from keeps a hand value in colors.ts until it folds. drop says why a key goes without a role. reserved names tokens, or prefixes ending in *, that nothing reads yet and are kept for a reader to come. interface lists the roles the palette names its keys after: a key reading one carries its name, in both themes, so no role has a second name.",
